<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Northern Frontier District</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Northern Frontier District was a vast, arid region of northern Kenya under British rule, inhabited largely by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oromo">Oromo</a> pastoralists. A British commission found in 1962 that most of its Somali population wished to join <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a>, but the territory stayed with Kenya at independence in 1963. Somali secessionists, backed by Somalia, then fought the Shifta War of 1963–1967 against the Kenyan government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/northern-frontier-district.jpg" alt="Northern Frontier District" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: JoeJohnson2 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Northern_Frontier_District_(NFD)_Flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
